{"name":"Good Karma","hex":"#333c76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"good","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person or an animal:\nActing in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral.","Acting in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good"},{"term":"karma","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sum total of a person's actions, which determine the person's next incarnation in samsara, the cycle of death and rebirth.","A force or law of nature which causes one to reap what one sows; destiny; fate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/karma"}],"entries":[{"title":"Good Karma","blocks":[{"text":"Good Karma is the tenth studio album by Roxette, a Swedish pop rock duo consisting of Marie Fredriksson and Per Gessle. Released on 3 June 2016 by Roxette Recordings and Parlophone, it was the only album issued by the duo under an international recording contract signed with Parlophone's parent company Warner Music Group. The album was produced by Gessle alongside Christoffer Lundquist and Clarence Öfwerman, with co-production on several tracks by Addeboy vs. Cliff, among others."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Roxette_-_Good_Karma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Karma","wikidata":"Q23759262"},{"title":"Karma","blocks":[{"text":"Karma is an ancient Indian concept that refers to an action, work, or deed, and its effect or consequences. In Indian religions, the term more specifically refers to a principle of cause and effect, often descriptively called the principle of karma, wherein individuals' intent and actions (cause) influence their future (effect): Good intent and good deeds contribute to good karma and happier rebirths, while bad intent and bad deeds contribute to bad karma and worse rebirths. In some scriptures, however, there is no link between rebirth and karma."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/EndlessKnot03d.png/330px-EndlessKnot03d.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karma","wikidata":"Q132196"},{"title":"Good","blocks":[{"text":"In most contexts, the concept of good denotes the conduct that should be preferred when posed with a choice between possible actions. Good is generally considered to be the opposite of evil. The meaning and etymology of the term and its associated translations among ancient and contemporary languages show substantial variation in its inflection and meaning, depending on circumstances of place and history, or of philosophical or religious context."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good","wikidata":"Q15290"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Roxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg/500px-Roxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Roxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg/1280px-Roxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Roxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg/500px-Roxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Per Gessle (left) and Marie Fredriksson (right) photographed in 2014, the same year they began recording Good Karma.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoxette_2014-04-08_003.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Hand_made_prayer_wheel_from_Nepal.jpg/500px-Hand_made_prayer_wheel_from_Nepal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, 